
The Microsoft 365 Copilot Power-User Playbook
(May 2026)
Volume 3: Saved Prompts, Tips & Tricks, Standard Power
Automate, and the Wider M365 Productivity Stack
TL;DR
The single highest-leverage move for any user is to combine the Microsoft Copilot
Prompt Gallery (Microsoft / Your prompts / Team prompts tabs in Copilot Chat), Saved
prompts (hover any prompt → bookmark icon), Scheduled prompts (up to 10 per user,
GA since January 2026), and a shared SharePoint List “Prompt Library” rendered as
Prompt Cards via JSON formatting.
The biggest skill upgrade is meta-prompting: ask Copilot to interview you (“Ask me 5
questions before you start”), critique its own draft, rewrite your prompt, and force
structure. These four moves consistently outperform longer one-shot prompts.
The firm’s “no agents / no autonomous flows” guardrails still leave a rich toolbox:
standard-connector Power Automate flows, Copilot Notebooks with per-notebook
custom instructions and audio overviews, Copilot Pages, Researcher, Create, plus
the M365 productivity layer (OneNote, Loop, Forms, Planner, Whiteboard,
Stream/Clipchamp, Lists, Bookings, Viva Insights/Engage/Learning, Designer, Sway,
Power BI Copilot, Edge Copilot Mode).
Key Findings
1. The Prompt Gallery is the home base. Microsoft consolidated prompt-sharing into the
in-Chat Prompt Gallery with three tabs — Microsoft prompts, Your prompts, Team
prompts. The standalone “Prompts” Teams app Lindsaytshelton was discontinued July
15, 2025; saved prompts now live in the Microsoft 365 Substrate Data Store, tenant-
scoped.
2. Scheduled prompts are a hidden game-changer. GA since January 2026. License
required: Microsoft 365 Copilot. Limit: 10 per user. GitHub Backed by a locked-down
Power Platform “Microsoft 365” environment with fixed DLP — fully compatible with the
firm’s restrictions.
3. Meta-prompting outperforms one-shot prompts. Best patterns: “Ask me N questions
first”, “Echo back what you understood”, “Improve this prompt then answer the improved
version”, “List the 3 weakest claims and how I’d verify each”, “Critique your answer as a
sceptical reviewer”.
4. Notebooks ≠ Pages ≠ Loop. Notebooks (per-notebook custom instructions, podcast-
style Audio Overview, grounded only in references) for project research. Pages (built on
Loop, paste as live components) IW Mentor for joint drafting. Loop for ongoing
workspaces.
5. Standard-connector Power Automate is genuinely productive. Outlook, Teams,
SharePoint, OneDrive, Excel Online (Business), Approvals, Forms, Planner, To Do, Office
365 Users connectors alone enable email triage, attachment archival, approvals, status
digests, scheduled distribution, OOO handover, recognition flows, and Form-to-task
pipelines — no premium licenses, no Dataverse, no agents.
6. Verifying Copilot output is non-negotiable. Microsoft’s own guidance: outputs are
drafts; click every citation; never use for final regulated content.
